{
  "schema": "trueopen-model-registration-chain-v1",
  "contract": "Model manifest to projection to registration digest",
  "notes": [
    "Each vector chains the three model digests: manifest_hash = H_V1(TRUEOPEN_MODEL_MANIFEST_V4, manifest bytes), chain_projection_hash = H_V1(TRUEOPEN_MODEL_CHAIN_PROJECTION_V3, canonical projection), and registration_digest = H_V1(TRUEOPEN_MODEL_REGISTRATION_DIGEST_V3, canonical JSON of chain_id, chain_projection_hash, manifest_hash, profile_version, proposer_address).",
    "chain_id and proposer_address are those of model_profile_canonical_v3.json. The projection and registration digests are derived by the Node implementation (ModelRegistrationDigest). Node treats manifest_hash as opaque, so the manifest digest is the one model_manifest_v4.json publishes, re-derived here with the same H_V1 framing.",
    "manifest_projection lists which manifest member each projection field equals in the golden vectors. It is descriptive: the Keeper never reads a manifest, and a client that rebuilds the projection from a fetched manifest follows this correspondence.",
    "ParserRefV1 is written as {} when absent (the zero value) and as {\"name\": ..., \"version\": ...} when present; the projection keys are tool_call_parser and reasoning_parser. The parser names here are placeholders. Which parser specification a name and version select, and how a non-empty parser is written inside a V4 manifest (its tool_calling and reasoning_parsing blocks), are not defined by this contract yet; the parser vectors therefore pin the projection encoding only and are not linked to a manifest."
  ],
